# tests/play.script - a game through the keyboard: the first screen ("t": any key but Space
# or Enter shows the title), the title, level 1,
# running, a quicksave (F6), running on, a quickload (F9: back), a pause (Esc). Every step
# waits for the program's own console lines (tests/check.sh checks them and the pictures,
# taken only where nothing moves: the kid's runs are timed by the clock, not by the game)
0 wait prince: start
+800 t
+0 wait prince: title
+2500 {space}
+0 wait prince: level 1
+0 wait prince: text LEVEL 1
+4500 shot
+300 key right 900
+1500 {f6}
+0 wait prince: text QUICKSAVE
+600 key left 1600
+1500 {f9}
+0 wait prince: text QUICKLOAD
+1200 shot
+300 {esc}
+0 wait prince: text GAME PAUSED
+600 shot
+300 {esc}
+1500 shot
